# --- Bill of Materials -------------------------------------------------------
#
# ►► The fan below is ONE ILLUSTRATION of the method — NOT a shape to copy. ◄◄
# Every good gets its OWN unique structure, designed from how THAT good is really
# made. Do not force another good into a fan-like, motor-deep shape: a shirt nests
# at its collar, a masala pack at its spice blend, a repair kit not at all. Derive
# the tree from the actual product; it may look nothing like this fan.
#
# The DEFAULT shape is a REALISTIC MULTI-LEVEL tree — the way goods are actually
# made — NOT a fixed count of flat BOMs. The number of BOMs, the number of items,
# how deep it nests, and WHERE it nests all FLEX with the finished good. See
# SKILL.md > "Author the BOM tree" for the full method. The core rule per part:
#
#   Does the company MAKE this from other things, or BUY it finished?
#     MAKE  -> it is a SUB-ASSEMBLY: give it its own [[BOM]] block and recurse
#              into its parts. Link it into its parent's [[BOM.RM]] with
#              `child_bom = true`.
#     BUY   -> it is a LEAF: just a [[BOM.RM]] line, no block of its own.
#
# Build BOTTOM-UP: a child's [[BOM]] block MUST appear BEFORE the parent that
# consumes it (so it is published first). Go deep only in the 1–2 branches that
# are the heart of the product; let everything else bottom out fast.
#
# HARD CAP: the deduped unique-item set (every FG + sub-assembly + leaf, by name)
# must be <= 20. This is a server-load ceiling, not a guideline — 003 aborts and
# creates nothing if the tree exceeds 20. Keep the tree focused and reuse shared
# parts to stay under it. (The fan example below is 18 items.)
#
# Typing (keeps the downstream PO/sales scripts happy, whatever the tree shape):
#   - the TOP finished good is "Sell"
#   - every sub-assembly is "Both" (it is manufactured AND consumed as a line)
#   - every bought leaf is "Both" (purchased input, also resellable)
# A sub-assembly must use the SAME unit and price wherever it appears (as its own
# FG and as a child line). Reused names collapse to one inventory item.
#
# The worked example below is a 400mm table fan: 3 BOMs, 3 levels, 18 items —
# deep through the motor (Fan -> Motor Assembly -> Stator), flat elsewhere.
# (For a quick, non-realistic seed instead, a FLAT set of single-level BOMs is a
# supported option — see SKILL.md.)

# ---- Level 2 (deepest): STATOR — wound in-house from copper + core ----------
[[BOM]]
[BOM.FG]
qty = 1
unit = "Nos"
name = "Stator 400mm"
price = 480
type = "Both"

[[BOM.RM]]
qty = 0.35
unit = "Kg"
name = "Copper Winding Wire"
price = 315
type = "Both"

[[BOM.RM]]
qty = 1
